WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:01.631
- [Narrator] These are your
(playful music)

00:00:01.631 --> 00:00:05.386
best friends, so close that
they're practically family.

00:00:05.386 --> 00:00:08.533
Or should I say, literally
just like your family.

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:10.777
- Happy birthday!
- Surprise.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.471
- What me?!
(screaming incoherently)

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:15.337
- [Narrator] Every squad has the child.

00:00:15.337 --> 00:00:17.495
Not necessarily the youngest in age,

00:00:17.495 --> 00:00:19.325
but definitely in spirit.

00:00:19.325 --> 00:00:22.554
- Ah, it's the best day of my life!

00:00:22.554 --> 00:00:24.567
Ah, it's the best day of my life!

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:25.693
They have fried chicken here.

00:00:25.693 --> 00:00:26.916
- [Narrator] The child runs on the power

00:00:26.916 --> 00:00:30.056
of positivity without ever
running out of something to say.

00:00:30.056 --> 00:00:31.225
- I have something to say.

00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:32.288
As much as I love fried chicken

00:00:32.288 --> 00:00:33.974
I love hanging with you guys.

00:00:33.974 --> 00:00:35.714
- You know what, I think
we're ready to order.

00:00:35.714 --> 00:00:36.832
- Okay, what can I get you guys?

00:00:36.832 --> 00:00:38.758
- Hello, well what is your name?

00:00:38.758 --> 00:00:39.709
You all remember Kevin right?

00:00:39.709 --> 00:00:41.402
- Yes, welcome.
- No.

00:00:41.402 --> 00:00:43.784
- [Narrator] The child also
has the uncanny ability

00:00:43.784 --> 00:00:46.269
to turn any stranger, however strange,

00:00:46.269 --> 00:00:47.398
into a new friend.

00:00:47.398 --> 00:00:49.884
- So, can I get anyone something to drink?

00:00:49.884 --> 00:00:52.597
- Oh, you know, actually
a seltzer would be nice.

00:00:52.597 --> 00:00:54.473
- Keith, you're getting
the remote all greasy.

00:00:54.473 --> 00:00:57.143
Hand it over we're gonna decide
what to watch as a group.

00:00:57.143 --> 00:00:59.768
Keith no.
(bowl clattering)

00:00:59.768 --> 00:01:01.334
(glass clunking)
- [Narrator] And,

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.986
just like a baby, he
sometimes lacks the ability

00:01:03.986 --> 00:01:05.815
to fully control his own limbs.

00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:07.999
- Hah, look, that dude's just like a baby.

00:01:07.999 --> 00:01:09.689
- Yeah, it's like he lacks the ability

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:11.237
to fully control his own limbs.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.090
(both laughing)

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.729
- [Narrator] You protect
the child at all costs,

00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:16.965
because he's the most fun and
sweet friend you'll ever have.

00:01:16.965 --> 00:01:19.870
- I have just the thing
that'll help you feel better.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.203
- [Narrator] Then there's
the adult of the group.

00:01:22.203 --> 00:01:25.527
The one who's stuck in
peak mom and dad mode 24/7.

00:01:25.527 --> 00:01:28.731
- It's a gift card!
- Oh I love cards!

00:01:28.731 --> 00:01:30.466
- [Narrator] The adult's parental advisory

00:01:30.466 --> 00:01:33.095
instincts kick into high gear whenever

00:01:33.095 --> 00:01:34.718
a resolution needs to be reached.

00:01:34.718 --> 00:01:37.341
(both arguing)
- Guys, guys!

00:01:37.341 --> 00:01:38.619
Keith got to pick last time

00:01:38.619 --> 00:01:41.360
so we're gonna with Zack's choice.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:43.190
- Goody.
- The fuck, what about me?

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:44.359
- No, your show is super depressing

00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:46.096
and not appropriate for Keith.

00:01:46.096 --> 00:01:47.643
Which one's the search button?

00:01:47.643 --> 00:01:48.482
What?

00:01:48.482 --> 00:01:50.766
You can draw on your snapchats?

00:01:50.766 --> 00:01:52.213
- That's your Instagram story.

00:01:52.213 --> 00:01:53.717
- No, Instagram's for pictures.

00:01:53.717 --> 00:01:55.030
- [Narrator] And like many a parent

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.951
the ever changing social media landscape

00:01:56.951 --> 00:01:59.530
is never immediately
apparent to the adult.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:00.363
- Yes!

00:02:00.363 --> 00:02:02.349
I caught another punchy rockeye.

00:02:02.349 --> 00:02:04.585
Cash me outside, how bout dah?

00:02:04.585 --> 00:02:06.836
- Oh my God, you ruin everything.

00:02:06.836 --> 00:02:08.807
- Oh, excuse me, we're ready to order.

00:02:08.807 --> 00:02:10.823
I'd like the Ahi tuna salad,

00:02:10.823 --> 00:02:13.585
and this guy will get
the fried chicken combo--

00:02:13.585 --> 00:02:15.044
- [Narrator] But who cares
if you're a little behind

00:02:15.044 --> 00:02:18.226
the times when you're the
only one on top of your shit?

00:02:18.226 --> 00:02:21.039
- Yeah, I have several questions
about several of the items.

00:02:21.039 --> 00:02:22.170
So the fettuccine alfredo.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.669
- Eugene, is that the girl you like?

00:02:23.669 --> 00:02:24.880
- [Eugene] Oh my God, shut up.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:25.728
- [Keith] Eugene's got a crush?!

00:02:25.728 --> 00:02:26.759
- [Eugene] No, shut up.

00:02:26.759 --> 00:02:28.023
♫ Eugene's got a crush

00:02:28.023 --> 00:02:30.558
- No, seriously, can I get
another one of these please?

00:02:30.558 --> 00:02:32.419
♫ He's got a crush

00:02:32.419 --> 00:02:34.624
- [All] Cheers.
- Let's get shit-faced!

00:02:34.624 --> 00:02:35.839
(howling)
- [Narrator] You all know

00:02:35.839 --> 00:02:38.089
and hope to survive the teenager.

00:02:38.089 --> 00:02:39.306
The friend in your group who is

00:02:39.306 --> 00:02:42.172
awfully good at being awesomely bad.

00:02:42.172 --> 00:02:44.091
- Someone take this from
me, my body is gonna--

00:02:44.091 --> 00:02:44.924
- I gotcha buddy.
- Regret that in

00:02:44.924 --> 00:02:46.189
the morning, thank you.

00:02:46.189 --> 00:02:48.893
- Aw, that dude's body is
gonna regret it in the morning.

00:02:48.893 --> 00:02:52.360
- Oh yeah, his little
Benjamin Button body.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.439
(laughing)

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.754
- [Eugene] Hold my shit.
- [Zack] What?

00:02:54.754 --> 00:02:58.348
That was an Oscar
nominated movie, I don't--

00:02:58.348 --> 00:02:59.181
(blows thudding)

00:02:59.181 --> 00:03:00.142
- [Narrator] Although teenager is violent

00:03:00.142 --> 00:03:01.934
(blows thudding)
and unpredictable,

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:04.843
(screaming)
you can always rely on him

00:03:04.843 --> 00:03:06.057
